Subject: [PATCH] fix(update): fail closed on strict bare supervisor evidence
 [daveey]

Problem: real bare discovery admitted custom service gateways and unreadable supervisor evidence to the strict stop set (r7-red.log: 11 failures).

Why: strict discovery reused best-effort _supervisor_markers; failed MainPID/Restart or environment/cgroup reads could mean no supervisor. PID disappearance then did not prove the service disarmed. Root (happened): unknown evidence was conflated with unsupervised. Root (not caught): existing bare fixtures proved argv/home ownership but did not inject service probe and supervisor evidence failures.

Recurrence: follow-up to 6d6ec4612552, which closed ownership uncertainty but retained the best-effort supervisor predicate. Countermeasure: strict-only tri-state evidence, conservatively refusing all unclaimed service cgroups even Restart=no, with readable environment/cgroup required for session/root admission. Default helpers unchanged.

Proof: canonical run_tests.sh RED 11 failed/12 passed; GREEN regression 89 passed, 1 macOS-only skip across five files. Health: 0 blocking, 0 advisory. No actual services or process signals; local commit only.
